{"r":"xwl","lane":{"p":825,"e":[{"h":"خَالَ","t":["aor. ",[2,"يَخُولُ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"خَوْلٌ"],", ",[1,"He became possessed of"],[2,"خَوَل"]," [so I read, meaning ",[1,"slaves,"]," or ",[1,"servants, and other dependents,"]," in the place of ",[2,"خوال"],", an evident mistranscription, in the TA,] ",[1,"after having been alone."]," (TA.) ― -b2- ",[2,"فُلَانٌ يَخُولُ"],[2,"عَلَى أَهْلِهِ"],[1,"Such a one pastures for his family:"]," (S:) or ",[2,"يَخُولُ عَلَيْهِمْ"]," signifies ",[1,"he milks and waters and pastures for them."]," (T, TA.) And ",[2,"خال عَلَيْهِمْ"],[1,"He ruled,"]," or ",[1,"governed, them."]," (JK.) And ",[2,"خال"],[2,"مَالَهُ"],", (K, * TA,) aor. as above, (TA,) inf. n. ",[2,"خَوْلٌ"]," and ",[2,"خِيَالٌ"],", (K,) ",[1,"He pastured his cattle,"]," or ",[1,"camels &c., and managed them,"]," or ",[1,"tended them, and sustained them,"]," (K, * TA,) ",[1,"well:"]," (K:) or ",[2,"خُلْتُ"],[2,"المَالَ"],", aor. ",[2,"أَخُولُ"],", ",[1,"I managed the cattle,"]," &c., ",[1,"well:"]," (S:) and ",[2,"خال عَلَى المَالِ"],", aor. ",[2,"يَخُولُ"],", ",[1,"he pastured the cattle,"]," &c., ",[1,"and managed them well;"]," as also ",[2,"خال"],", aor. ",[2,"يَخِيلُ"],". (TA in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".) -A2- ",[2,"خال"],", aor. ",[2,"يَخُولُ"]," and ",[2,"يَخَالُ"]," or ",[2,"يَخِيلُ"],", see ",[2,"اختال"]," (with which it is syn.) in art. ",[2,"خيل"],"."],"f":"1"},{"h":"خوّلهُ ٱللّٰهُ الشَّىْءَ","t":["(JK, S,) or ",[2,"مَالًا"],", (Msb,) or ",[2,"المَالَ"],", (K,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَخْوِيلٌ"],", (S,) ",[1,"God made him to possess,"]," (JK, S,) or ",[1,"gave him,"]," (Msb, K,) or ",[1,"conferred upon him, as a favour,"]," (K,) ",[1,"the thing,"]," (JK, S,) or ",[1,"property,"]," (Msb,) or ",[1,"the property."]," (K.) So in the Kur vi. 94 and xxxix. 11 [and 50]. (TA.)"],"f":"2"},{"h":"أَخْوَلَ","t":["(JK, Msb, K) and ",[2,"أُخْوِلَ"]," (K) ",[1,"He"]," (a man, JK, Msb) ",[1,"had maternal uncles:"]," (JK, K:) or ",[1,"he had many maternal uncles:"]," (Msb:) [both signify the same accord. to the K: but the latter properly signifies ",[1,"he was made to have maternal uncles,"]," or ",[1,"many maternal uncles:"]," see ",[2,"مُخْوَلٌ"],".] -A2- ",[2,"مِنَ الخَيْرِ"]," ↓ ",[2,"اخال فيه خَالًا"],[1,"He perceived,"]," or ",[1,"discovered, in him an indication,"]," or ",[1,"a symptom, sign, mark,"]," or ",[1,"token, of good;"]," as also ↓ ",[2,"تخوّل"]," (JK, S, K) and ",[2,"تخيّل"],". (K.) [See also 2 in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".] -A3- See also 10, in two places."],"f":"4"},{"h":"تَخَوَّلَ","t":["see 4: -A2- and see also 10, in three places. -A3- ",[2,"تخوّلهُ"]," also signifies ",[1,"He paid frequent attention,"]," or ",[1,"returned time after time,"]," (JK, S, K,) ",[1,"to it,"]," (JK,) or ",[1,"to him;"]," syn. ",[2,"تَعَهَّدَهُ"],". (JK, S, K.) You say, ",[2,"تَخَوَّلْتُهُمْ بِالمَوْعِظَةِ"],[1,"I paid frequent attention to them with exhorting,"]," or ",[1,"admonishing;"]," syn. ",[2,"تَعَهَّدْتُهُمْ"],". (Msb.) It is said in a trad., of the Prophet, ",[2,"كَانَ يَتَخَوَّلُنَا بِالمَوْعِظَةِ مَخَافَةَ السَّآمَةِ"]," [",[1,"He used to pay frequent attention to us with exhorting,"]," or ",[1,"admonishing, for fear of loathing"]," on our part, or ",[1,"disgust"],"]; (S;) or ",[2,"يَتَخَوَّلُهُمْ"],", i. e. ",[2,"يَتَعَهَّدُهُمْ"],": (TA:) As used to say ",[2,"يَتَخَوَّنُنَا"],", i. e. ",[2,"يَتَعَهَّدُنَا"],"; (S;) or ",[2,"يَتَخَوَّنُهُمْ"],": and some read ",[2,"يَتَحَوَّلُهُمْ"],", with the unpointed ",[2,"ح"],", explained in art. ",[2,"حول"],". (TA.) And sometimes they said, ",[2,"تخوّلتِ"],", ",[2,"الرِّيحُ الأَرْضَ"],", i. e. ",[2,"تَعَهَّدَتْهَا"]," [app. meaning ",[1,"The wind returned to the land time after time"],"]. (S.)"],"f":"5"},{"h":"اِسْتَخْوَلَهُمْ","t":[[1,"He took them as"],[2,"خَوَل"],", (K, TA,) i. e. ",[1,"slaves,"]," or ",[1,"servants, and other dependents."]," (TA.) -A2- ",[2,"استخول فِيهِمْ"]," and ",[2,"استخال"],[1,"He took,"]," or ",[1,"adopted, them as maternal uncles:"]," and ",[2,"خَالًا"]," ↓ ",[2,"تخوّل"],[1,"he took,"]," or ",[1,"adopted, a maternal uncle;"]," (K;) like as one says, ",[2,"تَعَمَّمَ عَمًّا"],": and ↓ ",[2,"تَخَوَّلَتْهُ"],[1,"She called him her maternal uncle."]," (TA.) You say, ",[2,"اِسْتَخِلْ"],[2,"خَالًا غَيْرَ خَالِكَ"]," and ",[2,"اِسْتَخْوِلْ"]," (JK, S) and ↓ ",[2,"تَخَوَّلَ"]," (JK) ",[1,"Adopt thou a maternal uncle other than thy"]," [proper] ",[1,"maternal uncle."]," (JK, * S.) -A3- ",[2,"الاِسْتِخْوَالُ"]," is also like ",[2,"الاِسْتِخْبَالُ"]," [as meaning ",[1,"The asking"]," one ",[1,"to lend"]," cattle, or camels &c.: and ↓ ",[2,"الإِخْوَالُ"]," is like ",[2,"الإِخْبَالُ"]," as meaning ",[1,"The lending"]," cattle, or camels &c.]: and AO used to recite thus the saying of Zuheyr: ↓ ",[2,"هُنَالَكَ إِنْ يُسْتَخْوَلُوا المَالَ يُخْوِلُوا"]," [",[1,"There, if they be asked to lend cattle, they lend"],"]. (S, TA. [See also 10 in art. ",[2,"خبل"],".])"],"f":"10"},{"h":"خَالٌ","t":[[1,"A maternal uncle;"]," one's ",[1,"mother's brother:"]," (JK, S, K:) pl. ",[2,"أَخْوَالٌ"]," (S, Msb, K) and ",[2,"أَخْوِلَةٌ"],", (K,) [both pls. of pauc.,] the latter anomalous, (TA,) and (of mult., TA) ",[2,"خُوَّلٌ"]," and ",[2,"خُؤُولٌ"]," (K) and ",[2,"خُؤُولَةٌ"],": (Msb, K:) the fem. is ",[2,"خَالَ"],", (JK, S, K,) ",[1,"a maternal aunt;"]," one's ",[1,"mother's sister:"]," (JK, S:) and the pl. of this is ",[2,"خَالَاتٌ"],". (Msb.) One says, ",[2,"هُمَاٱبْنَا خَالَةٍ"]," [meaning ",[1,"Each of them two is a son of a maternal aunt of the other"],"]; but one cannot say, ",[2,"ٱبْنَا عَمَّةٍ"],": (K:) and in like manner one says, ",[2,"ٱبْنَا عَمًّ"],"; but one cannot say, ",[2,"ٱبْنَا خَالٍ"],". (TA.) -A2- ",[1,"An owner"]," of a horse: you say, ",[2,"أَنَا خَالُ هٰذَا الفَرَسِ"],[1,"I am the owner of this horse."]," (K.) [See also ",[2,"خَالٌ"]," in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".] ― -b2- ",[2,"هُوَ خَالُ مَالٍ"]," and ",[2,"مَالٍ"]," ↓ ",[2,"خَائِلُ"],[1,"He is a manager,"]," or ",[1,"tender, of cattle,"]," or ",[1,"camels &c.;"]," (K;) or ",[1,"a good manager"]," or ",[1,"tender thereof;"]," (S, K; *) and so ",[2,"مَالٍ"]," ↓ ",[2,"خَوْلِىُّ"],": (S:) ↓ ",[2,"خَائِلٌ"]," signifies also ",[1,"a keeper,"]," or ",[1,"guardian,"]," of a thing; (T, S;) or ",[1,"a pastor;"]," (Fr, TA;) ",[1,"a people's pastor, who milks and waters and pastures for them;"]," and ",[1,"one who pays frequent attention to a thing, puts it into a good"]," or ",[1,"right state,"]," or ",[1,"restores it to such a state, and undertakes the management of it:"]," (T, TA:) ",[2,"خُوَّلٌ"]," [is a pl. of ",[2,"خَائِلٌ"],", like as ",[2,"نُوَّمٌ"]," is of ",[2,"نَائِمٌ"],", &c., and] signifies ",[1,"pastors who take care of cattle,"]," or ",[1,"camels &c.:"]," (TA:) and ↓ ",[2,"خَوْلِىٌّ"],", (K,) or, accord. to the M, ↓ ",[2,"خَوَلِىٌّ"],", (TA,) signifies ",[1,"a pastor who is a good manager of cattle,"]," or ",[1,"camels, and sheep or goats;"]," (M, K, * TA;) or ",[1,"a good manager and orderer of the affairs of men;"]," (TA;) and its pl. [or quasi-pl. n. or n. un.] is ↓ ",[2,"خَوَلٌ"],"; (M, K;) accord. to the M, like as ",[2,"عَرَبٌ"]," is of ",[2,"عَرَبِىٌّ"],". (TA.) [See also ",[2,"خَالٌ"]," in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".] -A3- ",[1,"An indication,"]," or ",[1,"a symptom, sign, mark,"]," or ",[1,"token,"]," of good (S, * K, TA) in a person. (S, TA.) See 4. -A4- ",[1,"A mole;"]," i. e. [",[1,"a thing resembling"],"] ",[1,"a pimple in the face, inclining to blackness:"]," dim. ↓ ",[2,"خُوَيْلٌ"]," and ",[2,"خُيَيْلٌ"],": and pl. ",[2,"خِيلَانٌ"],". (JK. [See also art. ",[2,"خيل"],".]) -A5- The [",[1,"kind of banner called"],"] ",[2,"لِوَآء"],", ",[1,"of an army"]," or ",[1,"a military force."]," (S, K. [See also art. ",[2,"خيل"],".]) ― -b2- ",[1,"A kind of soft garment,"]," or ",[1,"cloth, of the fabric of El-Yemen:"]," (JK:) ",[1,"a kind of"],[2,"بُرْد"],", (S, K,) ",[1,"well known,"]," (K,) ",[1,"having a red"]," [or ",[1,"brown"],"] ",[1,"ground, with black lines"]," or ",[1,"stripes."]," (TA. [Mentioned also in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".]) -A6- ",[1,"A black stallion-camel."]," (IAar, K. [See also art. ",[2,"خيل"],".])"]},{"h":"خَوَلٌ","t":["A man's ",[1,"slaves,"]," or ",[1,"servants, and other dependents:"]," (S, Msb, TA:) or ",[1,"slaves, and cattle,"]," or ",[1,"camels &c.:"]," (JK:) or the ",[1,"cattle, camels &c.,"]," [in the CK, ",[2,"النِّعَم"]," is erroneously put for ",[2,"النَّعَم"],",] ",[1,"and male and female slaves, and other dependents, given to one by God:"]," (K:) said to be (S) from 2 [q. v.]: (JK, S, TA:) it is said to be a quasi-pl. n.; (TA;) and the sing. is ↓ ",[2,"خَائِلٌ"],"; (S, K, TA;) though used as sing. and pl., and masc. and fem.: (K:) sometimes used as a sing. applied to ",[1,"a male slave"]," and ",[1,"a female slave:"]," but Fr says that it is pl. [or quasi-pl. n.] of ↓ ",[2,"خَائِلٌ"]," meaning ",[1,"a pastor."]," (S.) You say ",[2,"هٰؤُلَآءِ خَوَلُ فُلَانٍ"],", meaning ",[1,"These are persons who have been subjected, and taken as slaves, by such a one."]," (TA.) ― -b2- See also ",[2,"خَالٌ"],". ― -b3- Also ",[1,"A gift,"]," or ",[1,"gifts:"]," [and this seems to be the primary signification; whence “ a slave ” &c., and “ slaves ” &c., as being given by God:] so in the phrase, ",[2,"هُوَ كَثرُ الخَوَلِ"]," [",[1,"He is a person of many gifts"],"]. (TA.) -A2- Accord. to Lth, (TA,) it signifies also The ",[1,"lower part"]," (",[2,"أَصْل"],") ",[1,"of the"],[2,"فَأْس"]," [q. v.] ",[1,"of a bit:"]," (JK, K, TA:) but Az says, “ I know not the ",[2,"خول"]," of the bit nor what it is. (TA.) [See ",[2,"خَالٌ"],", last sentence but one, in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".]"]},{"h":"خَوْلَةٌ","t":[[1,"A female gazelle."]," (IAar, K.)"]},{"h":"خَوْلِىٌّ","t":[": see ",[2,"خَالٌ"],", in two places. ― -b2- Also ",[1,"A measurer of land with the measuring-cane."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"خَوَلِىٌّ","t":[": see ",[2,"خَالٌ"],"."]},{"h":"خُوَيْلٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"خَالٌ"],", of which it is the dim."]},{"h":"خُؤُولَةٌ","t":["The ",[1,"relationship of a maternal uncle"]," [and ",[1,"of a maternal aunt"],"]: (JK, S, K, TA:) an inf. n. (JK, TA) having no verb. (TA.) You say, ",[2,"بَيْنِى وَ بَيْنَهُ خُؤُولَةٌ"]," [",[1,"Between me and him is a relationship of maternal uncle"],"]. (S, K.) -A2- Also a pl. of ",[2,"خَالٌ"]," in the first of the senses assigned to the latter above. (Msb, K.)"]},{"h":"خَوَّالٌ","t":[[1,"A giver of many gifts."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"خَائِلٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"خَالٌ"],", in two places: ― -b2- and ",[2,"خَوَلٌ"],", also in two places."]},{"h":"تَطَايَرَ الشَّرَرُ أَخْوَلَ أَخْوَلَ","t":[[1,"The sparks flew about scattered;"]," meaning the sparks that fly about from hot iron when it is beaten; as in a verse of Dábi [El-Burjumee] cited in art. ",[2,"سقط"],": see 3 in that art. (S.) And ",[2,"ذَهَبُو أَخْوَلَ أَخْوَلَ"],[1,"They went away scattered,"]," (JK, S, K,) ",[1,"one after another, like as sparks are scattered from iron: "]," or, as some say, ",[2,"الأَخْوَلُ"]," itself means ",[1,"sparks: "],"(JK:) [but here,] ",[2,"اخول اخول"]," are two nouns made into one, and indecl., with fet-h for the termination: (S:) Sb says that they may be like ",[2,"شَغَرَ بَغَرَ"],", or like ",[2,"يَوْمَ يَوْمَ"],". (TA.) -A2- ",[2,"هُوَ أَخْوَلُ مِنْ فُلَانٍ"],[1,"He is prouder than such a one."]," (Suh, TA.) [See also ",[2,"أَخْيَلُ"],", in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".]"]},{"h":"مُخَالٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"مُخْوَلٌ"],"."]},{"h":"مَخُولٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَخْيَلٌ"],", in art. ",[2,"خيل"],"."]},{"h":"مُخْوَلٌ","t":["and ↓ ",[2,"مُخْوِلٌ"]," A man ",[1,"having maternal uncles: "],"(TA:) or the former signifies a man ",[1,"made to have many maternal uncles;"]," and ↓ the latter, ",[1,"having many maternal uncles: "]," (Msb:) and ",[2,"رَجُلٌ مُعَمٌّ مُخْوَلٌ"]," (Msb, K) and ↓ ",[2,"مُخَالٌ"],", (JK, K,) and ↓ ",[2,"مُعِمٌّ مُخْوِلٌ"],", ",[1,"A man who has generous paternal and maternal uncles:"]," (Msb, K:) but As disallows ",[2,"مُعِمٌّ"]," and ↓ ",[2,"مُخْوِلٌ"],": (Msb:) and the latter word in each case is not used, (K,) or is scarcely ever used, (TA,) without the former. (K, TA.)"]},{"h":"مُخْوِلٌ","t":[": see what next precedes, in four places."]},{"h":"إِنَّهُ لَمَخِيلٌ لِلْخَيْرِ","t":["(K in this art.,) or ",[2,"مُخِيلٌ"],", (S in art. ",[2,"خيل"],",) ",[1,"Verily he is adapted"]," or ",[1,"disposed by nature to good"]," [i. e. ",[1,"to be,"]," or ",[1,"to do,"]," or ",[1,"to effect,"]," or ",[1,"to produce, what is good"],"]. (S, K.) [See also ",[2,"مُخِيلٌ"]," in art. ",[2,"خيل"],".]"]}]},"maqayis":["الخاء والواو واللام أصل واحد يدل على تعهد الشيء. من ذلك: \" إنه كان يتخولهم بالموعظة \"، أي كان يتعهدهم بها. وفلان خولي مال، إذا كان يصلحه. ومنه: خولك الله مالا، أي أعطاكه ; لأن المال يتخول، أي يتعهد. ومنه خول الرجل، وهم حشمه. أصله أن الواحد خائل، وهو الراعي. يقال فلان يخول على أهله، أي يرعى عليهم. ومن فصيح كلامهم: تخولت الريح الأرض، إذا تصرفت فيها مرة بعد مرة."],"mufradat":["قوله تعالى: وتركتم ما خولناكم وراء ظهوركم [الأنعام/ 94] ، أي: ما أعطيناكم، والتخويل في الأصل: إعطاء الخول، وقيل: إعطاء ما يصير له خولا، وقيل: إعطاء ما يحتاج أن يتعهده، من قولهم: فلان خال مال، وخايل مال، أي: حسن القيام به. والخال: ثوب يعلق فيخيل للوحوش، والخال في الجسد: شامة فيه."]}